      "name": "galactosylceramide biosynthetic process",
      "aspect": "biological_process",
      "isObsolete": false,
      "definition": {
        "text": "The chemical reactions and pathways resulting in the formation of galactosylceramides, any composed of a ceramide backbone covalently linked to a galactose. The galactose can be sulfated or further elongated with one more monosaccharide often a sialic acid.",
